<h2>Which number belongs on a pair of leggings?</h2>
<p>An internal SKU helps you track stock. A GTIN identifies the trade item in a GS1-based supply chain. If your channel requires GTINs, assign them using the brand owner's approved process. Under <a href="https://support.gs1.org/support/solutions/articles/43000734083-how-many-gs1-gtins-do-i-need-when-i-have-a-product-with-many-sizes-and-colours">GS1's variant guidance</a>, a style offered in two colours and three sizes has six distinct size-colour variants. A supplier style code can be shared by all six; the GTIN cannot.</p>
<h2>Give the packing team a master sheet it can actually use</h2>
<p>Include your PO, style code, approved colour name or code, garment size, internal SKU, barcode number, barcode artwork revision, units per retail pack and label placement. Store barcode numbers as text so leading zeros survive the spreadsheet export. Do not send only a folder of artwork named “black-small”; it is too easy to reuse the wrong artwork when another style has the same colour and size.</p>
<p>For example, a black medium pair of leggings and a black large pair can use the same bag and label design, but each needs a separate row with its assigned identifier. If a top and bottom can also be sold individually, record those as separate sellable units from the two-piece retail set. Confirm the identifiers required for your own channel before printing.</p>
<h2>Approve the barcode after the garment is packed</h2>
<p>Scan from the surface the warehouse will actually handle. A label that scans on a desk can become harder to read after it is curved, covered by a seam, obscured by another sticker or placed under a reflective bag fold. Compare the returned digits with the sheet, then check that the digits resolve to the correct product in your inventory system. An audible beep by itself does not prove correct mapping.</p>
<p>Give the packing team a rule for reprints: who may release replacement labels, what revision they should use, and how obsolete labels are removed. Keep barcode placement separate from any care-label or market-labelling review. When requesting a <a href="/private-label/">Fitclo private-label quote</a>, send the sheet and placement example so label format, responsibility, sample approval and any extra costs can be discussed before packing.</p>
